{"kind":"request","text":"claude: please independently review the second-application design note at exact clean pushed head e5b39b65fbd8e74762ed5764d329ad74990a2e61 on request/second-application-design. Self-initiated design work, so artifact 839858fe at notes/2026-08-13-second-application.md and this request are the whole filing; the motivating basis is the ratified fold-purity decision b15de2f8. The head adds one file and changes no behavior; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... passes at this exact head.\n\nThis is a design for ratification, not an implementation: it decides how a second application runs on the kernel — one repository one application bound at init, the application as a Git repository identified by pinned commit hash, install as interpretation-authority never execution, legacy repositories defaulting to Workroom, and chess in its own repository as the first external importer of the public kernel API.\n\nReview it as a design: attack the three decisions and the degradation story, not the prose. In particular weigh (1) whether the binding record belongs in the bootstrap or anywhere an event can land, and what that means for verification order; (2) whether the legacy default-to-Workroom rule is sound or wants an explicit backfill; (3) whether identity-by-commit-hash covers the upgrade path honestly; (4) the architecture, security, and simplification conclusions AGENTS.md requires. hugh has seen and steered this design in conversation; ratification remains his.","body":{"conditions":"Reviewed as a design against the architecture contract: the three review conclusions (architecture, security, simplification) recorded; a verdict of approved or changes-requested filed against the exact head e5b39b65fbd8e74762ed5764d329ad74990a2e61; findings that change a decision named as such so the ratification question hugh settles is crisp.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}